From 0484d1a5a1e592aab147a3c2225a02fe48285aa1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:59:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] generalized-bulletproofs: merge batch verifiers; split
 the multiexp over threads

A node verifies a block's FCMP++ proofs as one batch per pool thread, and
each batch ends in its own multiexp per curve. Every one of those multiexps
carries the full generator vectors (g_bold, h_bold, h_sum), so a node with
12 pool threads computes the generator terms its batches share 12 times
per block. These two functions let the caller run one multiexp per curve
instead; monerod uses them in a later commit, which carries the
measurements.

- BatchVerifier::merge adds one batch verifier into another meant for the
  same Generators: scalars on the same generator add, and the additional
  terms concatenate. The merged multiexp is the sum of the two. Each proof
  enters its batch verifier with its own random weight (verifier_weight in
  arithmetic_circuit_proof.rs), so verifying the merged batch verifier
  checks every proof either one held, except with negligible probability,
  as for any batch verification.
- Generators::verify_split (std only) computes the same terms as verify,
  cut into up to `parts` disjoint chunks of at least 1,024 terms, each on a
  scoped thread, and adds the partial sums before the identity check.
  Merging alone leaves one large multiexp on one thread and costs wall time
  (up to +35% measured); the split gets it back and more.
- verify is unchanged.

Bounds: merge first extends the shorter scalar vectors with zeros, then
adds element-wise. verify_split pairs scalars with generators exactly as
verify does (zip), so in both, scalars beyond the generators' lengths are
dropped.

Constant time: not applicable. Batch verification works on public data,
and verify_split is variable time, like verify.

Tests, in crypto/fcmps:
- merged_batch_verifiers: real proofs of 1, 2 and 1 inputs, at split 1, 2
  and 4. Every single batch verifies, the merged batches verify, and a
  corrupted state fails alone and inside a merge (3 corruptions over both
  curves).
- merged_batches_reject_malleated_proofs: every single-byte malleation of
  real proofs (as test_malleated_proofs) that still passes the per-proof
  checks is merged between two valid batches, and the merged batch verifier
  rejects it, serially and split. The unmodified proof merged the same way
  verifies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
